{{Quote|Corporal, you and I will refuel in this fine establishment.|[[Meebur Gascon]] to [[WAC-47]]|<ref name="Missing in Action" />}}
'''Power Sliders''' was a [[Restaurant|diner]] located in the settlement of [[Pons Ora]] on the [[planet]] [[Abafar]]. It was owned by [[Borkus]], a [[Gender|male]] [[Sullustan]]. He employed [[Gregor]], an amnesiac [[Clone trooper|clone]] [[Clone commando|commando]], as a [[dishwasher]].<ref name="Missing in Action" />

At the time of the [[Galactic Civil War]], Gregor wore a muscle shirt with the symbol of his old workplace.<ref name="The Lost Commanders">{{Rebels|The Lost Commanders}}</ref> Decades later, the same symbol was used to decorate the [[flight suit]] of [[Hype Fazon]], a [[racer]] [[pilot]] on ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Space station|station]]. It was also printed on Fazon's racing starfighter ''[[Green Ace]]''<ref name="Bucket">{{SW|url=news/buckets-list-extra-the-high-tower-star-wars-resistance|text=Bucket's List Extra: 9 Fun Facts from "The High Tower" - ''Star Wars Resistance''|date=2018-10-29|quote=Nearly all of the logos on Hype's ship, racing outfit, and droid can be found in episodes of ''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' and ''Star Wars Rebels''. The "79's" cantina logo comes from ''The Clone Wars'' episode "Orders"; the "Power Sliders" and "Admiral Snackbar" logos were first seen on the planet Abafar in ''The Clone Wars'' droid arc; and several of the others can be found in background advertisements throughout the two series.}}</ref> and on the chassis of Fazon's [[astromech droid]] [[R4-G77]].<ref name="SW-Designing Star Wars: Star Wars Resistance">{{SW|url=news/designing-star-wars-resistance|text=Designing ''Star Wars'': ''Star Wars Resistance''}} {{C|Slide 12}}</ref>

